Tom: Really? What can it do that an ordinary house cannot?
Lucy: Well, it locks the door for us when we forget and leave.
Tom: That sounds useful. Does it save energy too?
Lucy: Yes. When everyone goes out, it switches off the lights by itself.
Tom: Amazing. How does it know when you are at home?
Lucy: It uses sensors to tell when we come in or go out.
Tom: I''d love to live in a house like that one day.', '露西一家刚搬进智能家居,很喜欢;汤姆问它有何特别之处;露西说他们忘锁门时它会替他们锁门;还能省电——大家外出时自动关灯;它靠传感器判断有没有人在家;汤姆也想住进这样的房子。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does Lucy''s family do recently?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["They moved into a smart home.","They bought a new car.","They built a garden.","They went on holiday."]},{"q":"What does the home do when they forget to lock the door?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It calls the police.","It locks the door for them.","It opens all the windows.","It rings loudly all night."]},{"q":"How does the home save energy?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It switches off the lights when everyone goes out.","It turns off the heating only.","It asks the family to leave.","It keeps the lights on all day."]},{"q":"How does the home know when someone is in?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It phones each person.","It uses sensors.","It checks the clock.","It asks the neighbours."]},{"q":"How does Tom feel about the smart home?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["He thinks it is useless.","He is afraid of it.","He would love to live in one.","He dislikes the idea."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective1', 'U2');
Dr Han believes that this time next year, more people will be travelling in driverless cars.
She also forecasts that robots will do much of our housework.
Vincent Black predicts that tiny robots will be helping doctors inside the body.
Both experts agree that we should welcome these changes rather than resist them.', '晚上好。今晚两位专家分享对未来的预测。韩博士认为明年此时会有更多人乘坐无人驾驶汽车;她还预测机器人将承担大量家务;文森特·布莱克预测微型机器人会在人体内协助医生;两位专家都认为我们应欢迎而非抵制这些变化。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is the topic of tonight''s programme?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["A new cooking show.","The history of cars.","A music concert.","Experts'' predictions about the future."]},{"q":"What does Dr Han predict about driverless cars?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["More people will be travelling in them.","They will disappear next year.","They will become more expensive.","Nobody will use them."]},{"q":"What else does Dr Han forecast?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Robots will only play music.","Robots will do much of our housework.","People will stop working.","Houses will become smaller."]},{"q":"What does Vincent Black predict?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Doctors will stop working.","Tiny robots will fly in the sky.","Tiny robots will help doctors inside the body.","Robots will replace all teachers."]},{"q":"What do both experts agree on?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["We should fear the future.","We should stop all new technology.","We should never use robots.","We should welcome these changes."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective1', 'U2');
Anna: I did. Some people now want to oppose these cars completely.
Ben: I understand their worry, but I''m not sure that is fair.
Anna: Why not? A passenger was hurt while the car was in driverless mode.
Ben: True, but most accidents today are caused by tired human drivers.
Anna: So you think the cars could actually be safer?
Ben: Yes, if we test them carefully instead of just rejecting them.
Anna: That makes sense. We should not stop new technology out of fear.', '本问安娜有没有看今早无人车事故的报道;安娜说有些人想彻底反对这种车;本理解他们的担忧但觉得不公平;安娜说有乘客在无人驾驶模式下受伤;本说如今多数事故是疲劳的人类司机造成的;安娜问那这种车会不会其实更安全;本说只要谨慎测试而非一味拒绝就可能更安全;安娜赞同,不该因恐惧而停止新技术。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What did Ben and Anna read about?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A driverless car accident.","A new music app.","A football match.","A weather warning."]},{"q":"What do some people now want to do?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Buy more such cars.","Oppose driverless cars completely.","Drive faster than before.","Build more roads."]},{"q":"According to Ben, what causes most accidents today?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Bad weather.","Broken roads.","Tired human drivers.","Slow machines."]},{"q":"What does Ben suggest doing with the technology?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Rejecting it at once.","Ignoring it completely.","Selling it abroad.","Testing it carefully."]},{"q":"What do they finally agree on?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["We should not stop new technology out of fear.","Driverless cars are perfect.","Nobody should drive again.","Fear is always right."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective1', 'U2');
It is true that artificial intelligence will do some routine work for us.
However, new technology usually creates more careers than it removes.
In the future, we will be needing people to design and repair these machines.
The best plan is not to fear the change, but to prepare for it.', '许多人担心智能机器会抢走工作;的确,人工智能会替我们做一些常规工作;然而,新技术通常创造的职业多于它取代的;未来我们会需要人来设计和维修这些机器;最好的办法不是惧怕变化,而是为之做准备。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What do many people worry about?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Machines will be too slow.","Machines will take away their jobs.","Machines will be too expensive.","Machines will never work."]},{"q":"What kind of work will AI do for us?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Only dangerous work.","All creative work.","Some routine work.","No work at all."]},{"q":"What does new technology usually do to careers?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["It removes every career.","It changes nothing.","It makes work impossible.","It creates more than it removes."]},{"q":"What kind of people will be needed in the future?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["People to design and repair the machines.","People who avoid machines.","People who sleep all day.","People who fear robots."]},{"q":"What is the best plan, according to the passage?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["To stop all machines.","To prepare for the change, not fear it.","To hide from technology.","To give up working."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective1', 'U2');
Leo: Voice commands? So you just tell it what to do?
Grace: Exactly. He says ''lights on'', and the kitchen obeys at once.
Leo: That''s clever. Can it cook for him as well?
Grace: It can warm the oven and tell him the moment the food is ready.
Leo: What if something goes wrong, like a water leak?
Grace: Then it detects the problem and sends a warning to his phone.
Leo: Wow. This used to sound like a fantasy, but now it''s real.', '格雷丝带利奥看她叔叔会听语音指令的新厨房;利奥问是不是直接吩咐它做事;格雷丝说叔叔一说''开灯'',厨房立刻照做;还能预热烤箱,并在食物做好时立刻告知;利奥问万一漏水怎么办;格雷丝说它会察觉问题并向叔叔手机发警告;利奥感叹这从前像幻想,如今成真了。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is special about the uncle''s kitchen?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It is very small.","It has no lights.","It understands voice commands.","It cannot be cleaned."]},{"q":"What happens when the uncle says ''lights on''?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Nothing happens.","The lights turn off.","An alarm rings.","The kitchen obeys at once."]},{"q":"How does the kitchen help with cooking?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It warms the oven and says when food is ready.","It does nothing useful.","It only plays music.","It hides the food."]},{"q":"What does the kitchen do if there is a water leak?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It ignores the problem.","It detects it and warns the uncle''s phone.","It floods the room.","It calls a plumber by name."]},{"q":"How does Leo feel about the kitchen?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It is boring and useless.","It is too dangerous.","It used to sound like a fantasy but is now real.","It is impossible to believe."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective1', 'U2');
It is being developed by a team of scientists at a famous university.
Like real bees, many RoboBees can work together as one group.
In the future, they may be helping with farming or finding people after a disaster.
The team believes that learning from nature is the key to building such machines.', '今天我们来看一种叫 RoboBee 的微型飞行机器人;它由一所著名大学的科学家团队研制;像真正的蜜蜂一样,许多 RoboBee 能作为一个群体协同工作;未来它们也许能帮助农业,或在灾难后寻找被困者;团队相信,向大自然学习是制造这类机器的关键。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is the RoboBee?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["A real bee.","A large farm machine.","A kind of phone.","A tiny flying robot."]},{"q":"Who is developing the RoboBee?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A team of scientists at a university.","A group of farmers.","A car company.","A single child."]},{"q":"How do many RoboBees work?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Each one works far away alone.","They work together as one group.","They never move at all.","They fight against each other."]},{"q":"What might RoboBees do in the future?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Replace all teachers.","Only sit in a museum.","Help with farming or find people after a disaster.","Drive cars on the road."]},{"q":"What does the team believe is the key to building such machines?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Using more metal.","Making them very large.","Keeping them secret.","Learning from nature."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective1', 'U2');

-- ===== 6) 写作 1篇 =====
